      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe, and I want to confirm it with you first.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, and the maximum for extended-release is 2,000 mg/day. A dose this high raises the risk of serious toxicity, including lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the usual maximum)\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals\n- **Another dose** (please tell me the dose and frequency)\n\nIf 1,700 mg three times daily is what you intend, tell me and I'll enter it with a note that you confirmed the dose. Otherwise, I'll enter the corrected order as soon as you reply."
      }
     ],
